WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.800
Using REau every day, with the bike and the dash

2
00:00:03.800 --> 00:00:08.267
1. Turn the bike on, open REau and tap Turn on

3
00:00:08.267 --> 00:00:14.200
If REau warns that Android Auto didn’t start, tap Open Android Auto settings

4
00:00:14.200 --> 00:00:19.267
In the three-dot menu, tap Start head unit server and go back to REau

5
00:00:19.267 --> 00:00:23.533
With the server on, REau shows Connecting and then Streaming

6
00:00:23.533 --> 00:00:29.600
With Android Auto Active and the dash Ready, put the phone away, even with the screen off

7
00:00:29.600 --> 00:00:35.933
2. With the bike stopped, set the destination in Waze, by voice or in the phone’s app

8
00:00:35.933 --> 00:00:41.400
3. To use Android Auto from the phone, tap Android Auto screen

9
00:00:41.400 --> 00:00:46.000
Tap and drag the picture to use Android Auto as in a car

10
00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:53.400
If Google Maps or the app menu opens, pick Waze. After using it once, it tends to open straight away

11
00:00:53.400 --> 00:00:58.600
4. Joystick, map mode: left zooms out and right zooms in

12
00:00:58.600 --> 00:01:02.667
Up is the dash’s back and center opens media control

13
00:01:02.667 --> 00:01:06.800
In media control, left and right move through the items

14
00:01:06.800 --> 00:01:10.867
Up opens the app menu and down calls Gemini

15
00:01:10.867 --> 00:01:13.467
And center confirms

16
00:01:13.467 --> 00:01:20.067
With Spotify on screen and playing, left and right change the song and center plays or pauses

17
00:01:20.067 --> 00:01:23.667
5. Call ringing: left answers

18
00:01:23.667 --> 00:01:26.267
Right and center decline

19
00:01:26.267 --> 00:01:28.867
Up and down do nothing

20
00:01:28.867 --> 00:01:32.933
On a call: right raises the volume and left lowers it

21
00:01:32.933 --> 00:01:35.533
Center ends the call

22
00:01:35.533 --> 00:01:38.133
Up and down still do nothing

23
00:01:38.133 --> 00:01:46.800
At the top of the dash’s picture you see who is calling and the volume. At the loudest level, a tap shows Call eight of eight again

24
00:01:46.800 --> 00:01:53.533
6. The info ring shows, one at a time, rain, wind, sun and the phone’s battery

25
00:01:53.533 --> 00:01:59.667
Each piece of information stays at least seven seconds: the time goes from seven to thirty

26
00:01:59.667 --> 00:02:04.333
Or, with Info in the title, they go in the gold band’s title

27
00:02:04.333 --> 00:02:09.733
With a route, the title shows twenty seconds of street and seven of information

28
00:02:09.733 --> 00:02:16.667
With the phone’s screen locked, the dash carries on as usual; only the preview inside the app stops

29
00:02:16.667 --> 00:02:27.067
7. If the dash’s Wi-Fi drops, REau warns you and comes back by itself when the network returns. When you switch the bike off, that is normal

30
00:02:27.067 --> 00:02:30.667
8. To stop, tap Turn off in the app

31
00:02:30.667 --> 00:02:33.600
Or tap Turn off in the notification

32
00:02:33.600 --> 00:02:37.400
Ride safe. On the road, eyes stay on the road

